{
  "id": "electric_motors___torque_vs__power_and_speed",
  "title": "Electric Motors - Torque vs. Power and Speed",
  "description": "Calculate and compare torque, power, and speed relationships for electric motors. Includes imperial and SI unit conversions with reference data tables for common motor ratings.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Electric Motors - Torque vs. Power and Speed\n\n**Work** is the result of a force acting over some distance. Work is quantified in joules (Nm) or foot-pounds.\n\n**Torque** is a rotating force produced by a motor's crankshaft. The more torque the motor produces, the greater is its ability to perform work. Since torque is a vector acting in a direction it is commonly quantified by the units Nm or pound-feet.\n\n**Power** is how rapidly work is accomplished - work in a given amount of time. Power is quantified in watts (J/s) or horse power.\n\nNote that the driving force of an electric motor is **torque** - not power. The torque is the twisting force that makes the motor run and the torque is active from 0% to 100% operating speed. The power produced by the motor is zero at zero speed.\n\n**Note!** that the full torque from zero speed is a major advantage for electric vehicles.\n\n## Equations\n\n**Torque in Imperial units:**\n- T(lbf·in) = P(hp) × 63025 / n(rpm)\n- T(lbf·ft) = P(hp) × 5252 / n(rpm)\n- 1 ft·lbf = 1.356 Nm\n\n**Torque in SI units:**\n- T(Nm) = P(W) × 9.549 / n(rpm)\n\n**Conversions:**\n- 1 hp = 0.746 kW\n- 1 lb·ft = 1.355 Nm"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "power_kw",
          "label": "Power",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "kW",
          "defaultValue": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "speed_rpm",
          "label": "Motor Speed",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "rpm",
          "defaultValue": 1500
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "torque_nm",
          "label": "Torque",
          "unit": "Nm",
          "formula": "inputs.power_kw * 1000 * 9.549 / inputs.speed_rpm",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "torque_lbf_ft",
          "label": "Torque",
          "unit": "lbf·ft",
          "formula": "inputs.power_kw * 1000 * 9.549 / inputs.speed_rpm / 1.356",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "torque_lbf_in",
          "label": "Torque",
          "unit": "lbf·in",
          "formula": "inputs.power_kw * 1000 * 9.549 / inputs.speed_rpm / 1.356 * 12",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "power_hp",
          "label": "Power",
          "unit": "hp",
          "formula": "inputs.power_kw / 0.746",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
